{
  "dom_id": "questionExplanation-76033",
  "name": null,
  "problem": "",
  "worked_solution": "The transformation $y=-g(x)$ reflects the curve $y=g(x)$ in the $x$-axis, as shown below.\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/capture/linear/14268132/assets/9a31e6ab638070920a2963fd630900820c12ee84bda0dc72e7d335d6601bd0d7.png)\n\nNote that for the function $y=-g(x):$\n\n- Its minimum value is indicated by the $y$-coordinate of the point $(-3,0),$ and this value is not included in the range.\n\n- Its maximum value is indicated by the $y$-coordinate of the point $(-8,5),$ but this value is included in the range.\n\nTherefore, the range of the function $y=-g(x)$ is $(0,5].$",
  "calculator_instructions": "",
